# IncidentIQ Agent — API Documentation

**Base URL:** `http://localhost:8080`  
**Authentication:** Bearer JWT (HS256)

## API Endpoints

| Group | Method | Endpoint | Authentication |
|---|---|---|---|
| Auth | POST | `/api/auth/register` | Public |
| Auth | POST | `/api/auth/login` | Public |
| Auth | GET | `/api/auth/me` | Protected |
| Incidents | GET | `/api/incidents` | Protected |
| Incidents | GET | `/api/incidents/{id}` | Protected |
| Incidents | POST | `/api/incidents/{id}/actions` | Protected |
| Incidents | PATCH | `/api/incidents/{id}/actions/{seq}/outcome` | Protected |
| Incidents | POST | `/api/incidents/{id}/resolve` | Protected |
| Incidents | POST | `/api/incidents/{id}/memory/retain` | Protected |
| Briefing | POST | `/api/incidents/{id}/briefing` | Protected |
| Briefing | GET | `/api/incidents/{id}/briefing` | Protected |
| Alerts | POST | `/api/alerts` | Protected |
| Service Catalog | GET | `/api/services` | Protected |
| Service Catalog | GET | `/api/services/{name}` | Protected |
| Feedback | POST | `/api/feedback` | Public |
| Feedback | GET | `/api/feedback` | Public |
| Demo | POST | `/api/demo/investigate` | Protected |
| Admin | POST | `/api/admin/seed` | Protected |
| Health | GET | `/api/health` | Public |

## Detailed Documentation

The complete API reference covers:

- Request and response body structures for every endpoint.
- Supported enum values: `Severity`, `IncidentStatus`, `Outcome`, and `MemorySyncStatus`.
- Field validation rules and constraints.
- Error response formats and HTTP status codes.
- Complete cURL walkthrough of the incident lifecycle:
  1. Register an account.
  2. Create an alert.
  3. Generate an incident briefing.
  4. Record an investigation action.
  5. Resolve the incident.
- Degraded-mode behavior when `GROQ_API_KEY` or `HINDSIGHT_API_KEY` is unavailable.

## Configuration

The application uses environment variables for external AI integrations:

- `GROQ_API_KEY`
- `HINDSIGHT_API_KEY`

Some functionality may operate in degraded mode when these integrations are unavailable.

## Running Locally

Start the Spring Boot application and access the API at:

`http://localhost:8080`

Check application health using:

`GET /api/health`

---

**Note:** Protected endpoints require a valid JWT access token in the Authorization header:

`Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN`
